{
  "version": "0.5.5-beta.6",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.5.5-beta.5`\n\n### Features\n\n- add a setting for the tab hover tooltip, off by default, since the tooltip with a tab's full title and connection popped up whenever the pointer crossed the tab bar; it covers both title-bar and split-group tabs and syncs with the other tab settings ([e5dfb085](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/e5dfb085e29763c96a6cf720b9a877c58583d9a0))\n- size the terminal log replay to its panel, with its own font size control and a Fit panel option on the toolbar, keeping the recorded columns and rows but never letting them overflow the panel, since the replay used a fixed font that left it small in a fullscreen window and the panel scrolled around xterm's own scrollback, and bring xterm's scrollbar up to date after each font change, since it only measures on resize or scroll and was left the wrong height and scrolled to the wrong line ([38952142](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/38952142a0be8244ba7f61fe289bf87caefc5b46))\n- put new terminal logs in a folder per day by default, with the template {year}-{month}-{day}/{profile}-{host}-{time}-{sessionId}, so a busy log directory stays browsable, while settings already saved keep their own template ([12400b86](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/12400b8601d8bbef5ad5557d4b0bb65d68869b82))\n\n### Fixes\n\n- keep a terminal log readable when quitting cuts its compression short, by writing the archive under a .partial name and renaming it once complete, removing unfinished and duplicate archives the first time the log directory is maintained, and reading a part from its plain file when both copies are left, since a truncated .gz beside its log used to duplicate the text or make the whole session fail to open, and the part was never compressed again ([70a65711](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/70a6571167af1b96a012b46b3727c6a7f337aca1))\n\n### Performance\n\n- write each session's terminal log on its own thread with buffered output, so logging never waits on the disk on the SSH task, the PTY reader or the main thread where keyboard input arrives, dropping output and noting a log_gap event only when 16 MiB is already queued, flushing at least once a second and fsyncing only on rotation or close, measuring disk usage in the background instead of walking the log directory on every status request, checking the size limit as logs grow, and waiting up to 3 seconds on quit for logs to write out ([e7b7dd83](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/e7b7dd8323dab2f86da7266f84ecab8112a7fcbd))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.5.5-beta.5...v0.5.5-beta.6](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.5.5-beta.5...v0.5.5-beta.6)",
